WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.440
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:11.460
Today we are going to create these cartoon-style&nbsp;
DeepFakes, and find out how much better this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:17.460
new AI is than previous techniques. I think you&nbsp;
will be very surprised when you see the results.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:26.400
So, what is exactly happening here? Well, in goes&nbsp;
a photo of us, and we also provide a target style,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:33.660
and bam. We become a cartoon, an anime&nbsp;
character, or a caricature of ourselves.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:39.780
That sounds absolutely amazing, so let’s&nbsp;
have a look at all three of these one by one.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:47.520
Now hold on to your papers, Fellow Scholars, and&nbsp;
let’s start with my favorite first. Caricatures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:53.640
These are meant to exaggerate the facial&nbsp;
features of the test subject and we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:01:00.180
also provide a style. Here, Mr Bean&nbsp;
has a funny face, and to my delight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:08.040
all of the caricatures also have a funny feel&nbsp;
to them. That is absolutely amazing. A+ work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:15.120
right there, little AI. Most of these also pass&nbsp;
the identity test - that is, if we were to cover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:23.160
the photo of the real person, and just look at the&nbsp;
AIs interpretation, in almost all cases, we could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:30.180
tell exactly who it is. That is absolutely&nbsp;
incredible. Just think about how difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:37.140
it is to retain the identity of the input photo&nbsp;
while transforming it according to this style.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:43.620
Also, glasses work. A variety&nbsp;
of hairstyles work. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:49.860
an AI that creates amazing caricatures.&nbsp;
This is incredible. Loving it.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:55.680
Two, next up, cartoons. The results&nbsp;
are still high-quality images,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.940
I like that. Glasses and&nbsp;
hairstyles are still supported.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:07.980
The identity test is still kind of okay here,&nbsp;
Harry Potter is definitely recognizable, in come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:15.840
cases, Mr Bean too. Traces of the stubble of Mr.&nbsp;
DiCaprio are visible on some of the results, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:22.320
they are gone from most of the rest, and hence,&nbsp;
it would be difficult to tell exactly who this is.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:28.140
Three, if we are looking to become&nbsp;
some anime characters, we see an even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:34.860
more powerful demonstration of this effect.
Sometimes it feels like our input photos are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:41.400
only taken into consideration to get the exact&nbsp;
position of the face, and hence I feel like we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:47.820
are seeing the same one character in different&nbsp;
poses. Now this will make a very interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:55.200
case study. Why? Well, perhaps the reason for&nbsp;
this is that these example images contain too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:02.040
few detailed facial features to be able to redo&nbsp;
a real person into an anime version. Remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:08.880
caricatures were extremely recognizable and&nbsp;
passed the identity test easily. So here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:16.680
I feel that we ran not into the limitations&nbsp;
of this AI, but into the limitations of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:24.240
concept itself. Actually, we can find&nbsp;
out about that ourselves. How? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:30.240
let’s compare this to what previous techniques&nbsp;
were capable of and see if this one is better.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:37.440
First, we can inspect these images ourselves.&nbsp;
These are three previous techniques, and this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:45.540
is the new method. Hmm. This one is called&nbsp;
GNR…Are you thinking what I am thinking? Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:53.760
this paper is called GANs N’ Roses. Yes, that&nbsp;
just happened. I am not kidding. This did not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:04:01.320
perform that well at all, but StarGAN2…this&nbsp;
is actually not so bad. In some cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:07.860
the quality of these images seems higher&nbsp;
than the new technique…until we realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:13.560
that is it not doing exactly what we asked&nbsp;
for. Remember, this is the input photo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:21.600
and this is the target. The input photo is meant&nbsp;
to be reimagined in the style of the target, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:30.720
oh yes, there we are. Sometimes, this just keeps&nbsp;
giving us images that are good, but good is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:36.360
good enough here. These would have to be close&nbsp;
to the target style, and often, they aren’t.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:41.640
Hence, I am really happy to see the&nbsp;
comparisons against the unsupervised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:47.760
image-to-image translation technique because it&nbsp;
is doing something very similar to this technique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:54.120
but the quality differences are quite&nbsp;
striking. The new one is so much better.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:05:02.820
Let’s see the user study from the paper and see&nbsp;
if others agree too. What? Is that really true?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:10.140
Goodness! That is one of the cleanest wins for&nbsp;
a followup paper I have seen in a while. Wow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:15.840
Just look at that! And the incredible thing&nbsp;
here is that all of these techniques were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:22.560
published in research papers from the last 2 to&nbsp;
3 years. These are from not so long ago at all!

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:28.860
You see, the progress in AI research is&nbsp;
nothing short of incredible. These amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:36.060
new papers are popping up every year, and in&nbsp;
some fields, almost every week. So, with that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.200
we can soon become any character&nbsp;
when playing in a virtual a world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:47.040
and we can also choose how much of our identity&nbsp;
we wish to reveal. What a time to be alive!

